  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#UK_gun_control_policy",
  "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
  "instance_name": "UK_gun_control_policy",
  "label": "UK Gun Control Policy",
  "description": "The UK has had strict gun control laws since the 1997 Firearms Act, which significantly restricted civilian access to firearms. The meme falsely implies that the UK 'gave up their guns' as a policy choice, which is misleading. In reality, the UK has never had a widespread civilian gun culture, and the 1997 Act was a response to the 1987 Hungerford massacre and the 1996 Port Arthur massacre in Australia, not a surrender of arms. The meme uses this false equivalence to criticize gun control policies.",
